 """Review queue CLI: list, confirm, or reject open review items.
 
+Triage Flow
+===========
+Every extraction with confidence < triage threshold (default 0.8) is automatically
+flagged via BuildingModel.flag_for_review() and appended to BuildingModel.review_queue.
+The auto-triage classifier (review_classifier.model.TypedDecider) assigns an urgency
+score (0-3).  Items with urgency >= 2 are surfaced first.
+
+Items with needs_review=True AND acknowledged=False BLOCK export via the export_gate
+in validate.py.  Acknowledging an item (--confirm) sets acknowledged=True; the
+export_gate then permits the export.
+
+Security Model
+==============
+Acknowledgment is recorded as an audit entry in BuildingModel.revision_log, tagged
+with the CLI identity (from MATCHLINE_IDENTITY env var, defaults to "cli").
+There is no server-side authentication for review queue access — control it via
+filesystem permissions on the model JSON.
+
 Usage:
     matchline review <model.json>                        # list open items
     matchline review <model.json> --show-all             # list all items
-    matchline review <model.json> --confirm <id>         # confirm item
-    matchline review <model.json> --reject <id>          # reject item
+    matchline review <model.json> --confirm <id>        # confirm item (clears export gate)
+    matchline review <model.json> --reject <id>         # reject item (removes from queue)
+    matchline review <model.json> --enable-auto-triage  # run auto-triage classifier
 """
 
 from __future__ import annotations
